        <mxCell id="ypKqzQfI5kiMkzrTepFO-10" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 36px;&quot;&gt;0.2&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="540" y="380" width="60" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ypKqzQfI5kiMkzrTepFO-11" value="&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-9163fa61-7fff-6b15-e16f-a394ba14f963&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;line-height:1.38;margin-top:18pt;margin-bottom:4pt;&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;docs: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TNqgmtKX7ZGl_O8MIWA73QrlZqSdwyDtLFTwsEmiUQw/edit?tab=t.0&lt;br/&gt;Push Payments (User-Initiated Transfers)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;In a push payment, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;customer initiates and authorizes the transfer of money&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;. The payer “pushes” funds from their account to the recipient’s account. This flow is common in systems like UPI, bank transfers, and even cryptocurrencies. The process typically involves the customer opening their banking or payment app, entering the merchant’s details or scanning a QR code, and specifying the amount. After verifying the request using secure methods like OTP, PIN, or biometric authentication, the payer’s bank debits their account and credits the merchant’s bank in near real-time. Push payments give customers complete control, are highly secure due to multi-factor authentication, and are best suited for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;peer-to-peer transfers, bill payments, or one-time purchases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;. However, they require user action each time, making them less ideal for recurring transactions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;Pull Payments (Merchant-Initiated Debits)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;In a pull payment, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;merchant or service provider initiates the transaction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt; after the customer has given prior consent, usually through a mandate or standing instruction. This model is widely used in credit card auto-debits, EMI payments, and subscription services like Netflix. Once the mandate is approved, the merchant’s system requests the bank or card network to debit the customer’s account on schedule, often without further customer interaction. Funds are then credited to the merchant after settlement. Pull payments simplify recurring billing and reduce friction for customers, but they require strict compliance and robust fraud protection, since merchants have the authority to initiate debits. This makes pull payments more efficient for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;subscriptions, utilities, and recurring bills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(255, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;, whereas push payments excel in real-time, customer-driven scenarios.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-1530" y="800" width="1090" height="390" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ypKqzQfI5kiMkzrTepFO-12" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0.997;entryY=0.713;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;exitX=0.019;exitY=0.41;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ypKqzQfI5kiMkzrTepFO-2" target="ypKqzQfI5kiMkzrTepFO-11">
